# Digital PIN — Design Framework & Roadmap

Purpose: A practical, shared blueprint for the public website, customer portal, and supplier portal—covering UX, design system, security, performance, and a 6‑week delivery path.

## 1) Goals & principles
- Clear, modern, fast, and secure experiences across all surfaces.
- One design language (tokens + components) with light/dark readiness.
- Least privilege and server-side API access; no secrets in browsers.
- Ship iterative value weekly with measurable KPIs.

## 2) Design system (upgrade-safe and shared)
- Tokens: colors (brand: #0f4c81, accent: #0ec5a1), spacing scale (4–32), radius (6–12), elevation, typography scale (12–32), transitions.
- Components (v1): Button, Input, Select, Textarea, Alert, Badge, Card, Modal/Drawer, Tabs, Table, Pagination, Breadcrumb, Navbar, Sidebar, Empty, Skeleton, Toast.
- Accessibility: color contrast ≥ 4.5:1, focus states, ARIA roles, keyboard nav.
- Tech: Next.js + TypeScript. Optionally Tailwind + shadcn/ui for speed; export a small ui package for reuse.

## 3) Information architecture
- Public site (digitalpin.online)
  - Home, Solutions/Industries, Pricing, About/Team, Contact, Blog/Resources, Docs/FAQ, Legal.
- Customer portal (app.digitalpin.online)
  - Auth (login/forgot, 2FA later), Dashboard, Invoices (list/detail/pay), Payments (history), Tickets (create/track), Reports (PDF/Excel), Profile/Organization.
- Supplier portal (suppliers.digitalpin.online or under app)
  - Auth, Purchase Orders (list/detail/confirm), Deliveries/GRN, Supplier Invoices, Tickets, Documents/Compliance, Profile/Bank.

## 4) Core UX flows
- Auth: rate-limit, lockout after failed attempts, CSRF, session httpOnly.
- Customer invoices: list → detail → pay → receipt → status sync.
- Tickets: create with subject/message/attachments → updates/notifications.
- Supplier: PO intake → accept/hold → ship/GRN → upload supplier invoice → reconcile.

## 5) Tech & integration
- Stack: Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript + Axios + Zod.
- APIs: Dolibarr REST via server-side routes only (DOL_API_BASE + DOLAPIKEY in server env).
- Shared UI: small local package or mono-repo workspace later.
- Environments: dev on port 3210; prod on app.digitalpin.online via Nginx reverse proxy.

## 6) Security (minimum bar)
- HTTP headers: CSP, X-Frame-Options=DENY, X-Content-Type-Options=nosniff, Referrer-Policy=strict-origin-when-cross-origin, HSTS in prod.
- Auth: next-auth with secure cookies (httpOnly, SameSite=Lax), rotating secrets, optional 2FA later.
- RBAC: scope views to owning thirdparty/supplier; enforce in server routes.
- Secrets: store only in server env files; rotate DOLAPIKEY periodically.
- WAF/logging: log sensitive events; rate-limit API routes.

## 7) Performance & SEO
- Budgets: LCP < 2.5s, TTI < 4s, CLS < 0.1.
- Assets: responsive images, WebP/AVIF, prefetch critical paths, code-splitting.
- Caching: ISR/SSG for public site; strong cache for static; no cache for API.
- SEO: sitemap, robots, meta/OG, Schema.org (Organization/Product/FAQ), 404/500 pages.

## 8) Cloudflare (rules we will set)
- SSL/TLS: Full (strict). Edge: Always Use HTTPS=ON; TLS ≥ 1.2; HTTP/2+HTTP/3=ON; enable HSTS only after HTTPS is verified.
- Cache Rules:
  - Bypass cache: `/.well-known/acme-challenge/*`, `/api/*`.
  - Optionally cache static of public site (respect Cache-Control headers).
- Security/WAF: don’t strip custom headers; DOLAPIKEY must pass to origin. Optionally allowlist office IPs for `/api/*`.
- Speed: Rocket Loader OFF for app and suppliers portals.
- DNS: enable orange cloud after certs are issued.

## 9) Ops & observability
- Logs/Errors: Sentry or OpenTelemetry; alerts on 5xx spikes and auth failures.
- Uptime: health checks for site and portals.
- Releases: blue/green or canary via Nginx upstream toggles; backups before major changes.

## 10) Timeline (6 weeks)
- W1: Design tokens + core components; skeletons for site and portals.
- W2: Public site MVP (Home/Solutions/About/Contact) + SEO/Analytics.
- W3: Customer portal Auth/Dashboard + invoices/tickets (read).
- W4: Payments + ticket create + export (PDF/Excel) + UI polish.
- W5: Supplier portal (PO/GRN/Invoice) + notifications.
- W6: Hardening, performance, observability, docs, staged launch.

## 11) Deliverables
- Design system docs + shared UI library.
- Public site production-ready with SEO.
- Customer portal: invoices/payments/tickets + reports.
- Supplier portal: PO/GRN/supplier invoice + tickets.
- Runbooks: deploy, Cloudflare rules, SSL renewal, backups.

## 12) Acceptance criteria
- Security headers present; no secrets in client; API calls server-only.
- Performance budgets met on Core Web Vitals.
- Role-based data scoping validated.
- Cloudflare rules in place; orange cloud enabled post-SSL.

